from .interfaces.edaemon import WTSEdaemonInterface
from .interfaces.egate import WTSEgateInterface
from .interfaces.wts import WTSInterface


class WTSsim(WTSInterface, WTSEgateInterface, WTSEdaemonInterface):
    """
    Introduction
    ************


    A library to work with WTS (Wraparound Test Solution) e.g. start/stop the egate binary file.

    This library is able to handle the edaemon/egate startup procedure and execute egate commands via the Telnet interface.
    User is able to use egate in the same way as manually, including lua execution.

    Library keywords are grouped like below:

    * Keywords to support edaemon operations contains edaemon word in the name
    * Keywords to support egate operations contains egate word in the name
    * Keywords to support WTS environment (egate and edaemon) contains wts word in the name


    Focused interface
    *****************


    WTS keywords are available to support most common cases available in UTE environment e.g.

    ::

        PC with UTE and WTS  --------------+---- eth4 ---> FSM (I-PHY)
             +- EGATE   (port: 20000)      |
             +- EDAEMON (port: 10000)      +---- eth3 ---> eNB (SUT)
             +- EDAEMON (port: 30000)

    Common startup procedure looks like below:

    ::

        cd /path/to/wts/binaries
        sudo ./edaemon --port 10000
        sudo ./edaemon --port 20000
        ./egate --port 30000
        telnet 0 20000
            cfg file=/path/to/configuration.lua
            start
            info
            reset
            shutdown
        sudo killall edaemon

    The same scenario is executed as default via WTS keywords:

    ::

        Start WTS appplications      cfg_file=/path/to/configuration.lua
        Start WTS services
        Execute egate command        cmd=info
        Stop and collect WTS logs

    To support custom environments like multiple PC's taf.sw.wtssim library provides egate and edaemon keywords. These keywords allow
    user to create custom startup/shutdown procedures and support more than only one fixed scenario.


    Extensions
    **********


    It is possible to extend library via **ext** argument. Any class provided as argument will be notified by taf.sw.wtssim about
    create/deleted egate with alias and egate instance. This allows user to create custom logic on top of existing egate and
    existing SSH or Telnet connection.

    **ext** parameter is available in keywords:

    * Setup egate
    * Start WTS applications

    **ext** parameter allows to specify one library/class as a string or multiple libraries/classes as a list.
    The import logic looks like below:

    * some_lib - taf.sw.wtssim expects:

        * some_lib package or module
        * some_lib class in some_lib package or module

    * some_lib.SomeClass - taf.sw.wtssim expects:

        * some_lib.SomeClass module or package
        * SomeClass in some_lib.SomeClass module or package
        * SomeClass in some_lib module or package

    This feature requires from extension package, module or class to implement methods:
    ::

        def egate_created(egate, alias):
            pass     # <-- Code here

        def egate_deleted(alias):
            pass     # <-- Code here

    Interaction between taf.sw.wtssim and extension is defined by few simple rules:

    * All entries without **egate_created** method will be skipped.
    * All entries without **egate_deleted** will not be informed that egate object was removed.
    * Extension classes cannot have arguments in __init__ method without default values.
    * Library disables all exceptions from clients which may appear during **egate_created** and **egate_deleted** method call.
      Exceptions are logged and ignored to keep the main features stable.


    Multiple instances
    ******************


    This library supports multiple setups where each can be specified by **alias** argument for every keyword.
    This argument can be specified as follows:
    ::

        Setup egate               egate_port=8888         alias=egate1
        Setup WTS applications    cfg_file=/some/file     alias=wts1

        :Multiple setups through aliases via kwargs:
            * **alias**   (string)   - Unique identifier for a certain wtssim instance. Default is none.

    :warning: Egate and WTS keywords share the same **pool of aliases**. Edaemon has separate **pool of aliases**.
              Aliases have to be unique inside each group.
    """

    ROBOT_LIBRARY_SCOPE = "SUITE"
    ROBOT_LISTENER_API_VERSION = 3

    def __init__(self):
        self.ROBOT_LIBRARY_LISTENER = self
        super().__init__()

    def _teardown_all_aliases(self) -> None:
        self.teardown_all_aliases_for_egate()
        self.teardown_all_aliases_for_edaemon()

    def _end_suite(self, *args, **kwargs) -> None:
        try:
            if not self.save_egate:
                self._teardown_all_aliases()
        except AttributeError:
            self._teardown_all_aliases()
